# MCP Endpoint Info

The MCP endpoint page gives the connection details for pointing any MCP-compatible AI client at AI Game Developer: the hosted endpoint https://ai-game.dev/mcp (Streamable HTTP; OAuth 2.1 browser sign-in, project keys written by setup-mcp, or personal access tokens for CI) plus per-client config snippets.

_Last updated: 2026-11-04_

## The fastest way: let setup-mcp write it

Every engine CLI writes the right config file for your client: the project-pinned URL plus a project key, so the client connects at once with nothing to sign in. Add --oauth for a URL-only config that signs in through the browser instead. The desktop app does the same when it sets up a project. Install guides: https://ai-game.dev/engines/unity, https://ai-game.dev/engines/unreal, https://ai-game.dev/engines/godot.

```bash
unity-mcp-cli setup-mcp claude-code ./MyUnityProject
unreal-mcp-cli setup-mcp cursor --path ./MyUnrealProject
godot-cli setup-mcp gemini ./MyGodotProject --oauth
```

## Signing in

### OAuth 2.1 — a browser sign-in, nothing to paste

Clients that support MCP authorization sign in through your browser on first connect (authorization code with PKCE and dynamic client registration), then keep their own tokens. The config holds only the URL. The engine CLIs’ own login command uses the device-code flow instead.

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "ai-game-dev": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://ai-game.dev/mcp"
    }
  }
}
```

### Project keys — what setup-mcp writes

A project key (agd_pk_…) belongs to one project and is sent as a bearer token with the pinned URL. setup-mcp creates it and writes it into the client’s config, so the client works without a browser sign-in.

### /mcp vs /mcp/p/<pin>

/mcp is the base endpoint — the server routes to one of your connected editors. /mcp/p/<pin> is pinned to one project and always reaches that project’s editor; setup-mcp writes the pinned URL. See the Authentication guide (https://ai-game.dev/docs/auth).

### Personal access tokens — for CI and scripts

For CI or a client that cannot open a browser, create a personal access token on your access tokens page (https://ai-game.dev/app/api-keys) and send it as a bearer token:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "ai-game-dev": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://ai-game.dev/mcp",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer [REDACTED]"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Supported clients

Per-client config snippets for 14 MCP clients, in the shape each client’s setup-mcp entry uses — the first snippet signs in over OAuth, "PAT" variants use a personal access token.

### Claude Desktop

Anthropic’s desktop app for Claude — first-class MCP client. Platforms: Windows, macOS. Client: https://claude.ai/download

`Settings → Connectors`:

```text
Settings → Connectors → Add custom connector
Name: ai-game-dev
URL:  https://ai-game.dev/mcp
```

### Claude Code

Anthropic’s terminal coding agent — MCP servers configured per project. Platforms: Windows, macOS, Linux. Client: https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code

`CLI add`:

```bash
claude mcp add --transport http ai-game-dev "https://ai-game.dev/mcp"
```

`CLI add · PAT`:

```bash
claude mcp add --transport http ai-game-dev "https://ai-game.dev/mcp" \
  --header "Authorization: Bearer [REDACTED]"
```

`.mcp.json`:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "ai-game-dev": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://ai-game.dev/mcp"
    }
  }
}
```

